msgid "Quarkus Update Tool - TL;DR"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 3 is out and we encourage our users to upgrade their applications to "
"experience the best Quarkus ever!\n"
"The team worked hard to deliver a lot of new features and performance "
"improvements.\n"
"But of course, there are also some breaking changes.\n"
"The https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.0[migration "
"guide] describes all the important changes in the core extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nevertheless, there is also some tedious work that needs to be done.\n"
"Quarkus 3 has updated to the latest Jakarta EE 10 APIs, which include the "
"infamous change of the `javax.\\*` to the `jakarta.*` packages.\n"
"If your application makes use of any Jakarta API, and there's a good chance "
"it does (think about JAX-RS, CDI, JPA, etc.), you'll need to modify your "
"code.\n"
"Furthermore, if there's an explicit Jakarta API dependency in the project, "
"you'll need to update this dependency as well."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Of course, you can migrate the application manually.\n"
"But since Quarkus embraces the developer joy there is the Quarkus Update "
"Tool to the rescue!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This blog post was written just after the Quarkus 3.0 release.\n"
"Things have evolved a bit since then."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information about how to update to the latest Quarkus, have a look "
"at the https://quarkus.io/guides/update-quarkus[dedicated guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also find all the migration guides in https://github.com/quarkusio/"
"quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guides[our wiki]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Install the https://quarkus.io/guides/cli-tooling[Quarkus CLI] or make sure "
"the latest version is installed"
msgstr ""

msgid "Run `quarkus update`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Check the changes made by the tool"
msgstr ""

msgid "Profit!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus Update Tool - The Full Story"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The goal of the update tool is to help developers to migrate an application "
"to Quarkus 3 smoothly.\n"
"The update process can be triggered from the Quarkus CLI, and directly via "
"Maven or Gradle commands.\n"
"The tool itself is basically a set of https://docs.openrewrite.org/"
"[OpenRewrite transformation rules].\n"
"Most of the rules are defined in the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus-"
"updates[Quarkus Update Recipes] project."
msgstr ""

msgid "What exacty does the update tool do?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Updates the Quarkus version"
msgstr ""

msgid "Transforms the source code to use the `jakarta.*` packages"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Upgrades the Quarkiverse extensions to the versions compatible with Quarkus "
"3.0"
msgstr ""

msgid "Updates the Java EE API dependencies to the Jakarta EE API versions"
msgstr ""

msgid "Adjusts some common dependencies (such as Jackson and Hibernate)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Transforms the configuration files for some configuration properties (for "
"example `quarkus.kubernetes.host` to `quarkus.kubernetes.ingress.host`)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renames some common service providers (for example `/META-INF/services/javax."
"ws.rs.ext.Providers` to `/META-INF/services/jakarta.ws.rs.ext.Providers`)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Let's get down to business.\n"
"To run the update:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Keep in mind that there is no dry-run mode.\n"
"In other words, once you trigger the update, the changes will be immediately "
"written to the file system.\n"
"However, you can leverage the source code management tool to see the "
"transformations applied.\n"
"For example, if using Git then run the update tool and execute the `git "
"diff` command afterwards to see the changes.\n"
"And if something went wrong then just use `git checkout .` to revert the "
"changes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"That's it.\n"
"Your application should be ready now.\n"
"If there's something wrong please, ping us on Zulip or file a https://github."
"com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[new issue]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this article, we discussed the possibilities of the Quarkus Update Tool "
"that will make your migration to Quarkus 3.0 a breeze.\n"
"Don't hesitate and go for it!"
msgstr ""

